  "strategy": "1. **Approach and Rationale**\n   - **Core Idea**: We adopt a hybrid optimization strategy combining global search (simulated annealing) with local refinement (projected gradient descent) at varying resolutions. The key insight is that lower resolutions better explore the search space, while higher resolutions enable fine-tuning. This overcomes gradient descent's tendency to get stuck in local optima.\n   - **Bottleneck Addressed**: The original algorithm relies solely on gradient-based methods with smoothing, which can easily converge to suboptimal solutions. Simulated annealing introduces stochastic exploration to find better starting points, and multi-resolution analysis prevents premature convergence.\n   - **Limitations**: The approach may have higher computational costs due to stochastic search and interpolation steps. However, the multi-resolution strategy mitigates this by focusing computational effort on promising regions.\n\n2. **Mathematical Specification**\n   - **Objective**: Minimize \\( C_5 = \\max_k \\int_0^2 h(x) (1-h(x+k))  dx \\)\n     - Computed as \\( \\max_k \\left( \\text{np.correlate}(h, 1-h, \\text{mode}='full') \\right) \\times (2.0 / n_{\\text{points}} \\)\n   - **Constraints**:\n     - \\( 0 \\leq h[i] \\leq 1 \\forall i \\)\n     - \\( \\sum h = n_{\\text{points}} / 2 \\)\n   - **Representation**: Piecewise constant on [0, 2] grid with \\( n_{\\text{points}} \\) samples.\n   - **Resolution Handling**:\n     - Start with \\( n_{\\text{base}} = 50 \\)\n     - Refine to \\( n_{\\text{base}} \\times 2 \\) and \\( n_{\\text{base}} \\times 4 \\) if improvement possible\n   - **Optimization Steps**:\n     - **Simulated Annealing (SA)**: \\( 30\\% \\) budget for global exploration\n     - **Projected Gradient Descent (PGD)**: \\( 50\\% \\) budget for local refinement\n     - **Interpolation**: \\( 20\\% \\) budget for resolution scaling\n\n3. **Implementation Procedure**\n   - **Phase 1: Low-Resolution Initialization**\n     1. Initialize \\( h_0 \\) with 50 random samples in \\([0,1]\\) clipped to \\([0,1]\\) and summed to 25\n     2. Compute initial \\( C_5 \\) using full correlation\n     3. Implement simulated annealing:\n        - Temperature starts at 0.5 and cools linearly to 0.1 over \\( 4000 \\) steps\n        - At each step: perturb \\( h \\) by uniform jitter \\( \\pm 0.1 \\) in \\( 10\\% \\) of positions\n        - Accept worse moves with probability \\( \\exp(-\\Delta C_5 / T) \\)\n        - After \\( 2000 \\) steps, if improvement < 1e-5, early terminate\n\n   - **Phase 2: Coarse-to-Fine Refinement**\n     1. If \\( C_5 \\) improved significantly, scale up to \\( n_{\\text{high}} = 100 \\):\n        - Interpolate existing \\( h \\) via linear resampling\n        - Project to feasible set: clip to [0,1] and adjust sum to 50\n     2. Apply projected gradient descent:\n        - Use smoothing technique with adaptive alpha\n        - Update rule: \\( h \\leftarrow \\text{proj}_{\\text{simplex}}(h - \\eta \\nabla C_5) \\)\n        - Linesearch with Armijo condition\n\n   - **Phase 3: Final Refinement**\n     1. Scale to \\( n_{\\text{high}} = 200 \\) if applicable\n     2. Add random jitter to maintain exploration pressure\n     3. Final SA cycle with decreasing temperature\n\n4. **Search Choices and Variations**\n   - **Cooling Schedule**: Linear cooldown from 0.5 to 0.1\n   - **PGD Parameters**:\n     - Initial learning rate: 0.01\n     - Min step: 0.0001\n     - Max iterations: 2000\n   - **Interpolation**: Linear interpolation between grid points\n\n5. **Compute Budget and Robustness**\n   - **Time Allocation**:\n     - Phase 1 (SA): 330 seconds\n     - Phase 2 (PGD): 440 seconds\n     - Phase 3 (Refinement): 330 seconds\n   - **Feasibility Checks**:\n     - Clip values outside [0,1]\n     - Adjust sum to target within 1% tolerance\n   - **Fallback**:\n     - If SA fails to improve, revert to parent solution\n     - Use gradient descent fallback if PGD diverges\n\n6. **Validation and Return Contract**\n   - **Feasibility Checks**:\n     1. \\( 0 \\leq h[i] \\leq 1 \\forall i \\)\n     2. \\( |\\sum h - n_{\\text{points}}/2| < 0.05 \\)\n     3. \\( C_5 \\) is finite\n   - **Return Format**: (h_values, C5_bound, n_points)\n   - **Final Checks**:\n     - Re-compute \\( C_5 \\) with fallback method\n     - Ensure resolution is power of two\n     - Validate integral using numerical integration",
